(*
Confinement pin: a class declaring only usingPlatform: platform cannot reach serial.
std-lib step 3c-3b. Empirical result: compile succeeds (serial is an unknown unary send),
but runtime aborts with DNU — "Message 'serial' not understood by receiver" — because the
receiver (the entry module instance) has no serial: slot. Compiler exit 0, runner exit 134.
This mirrors 33_string_not_collection.ns: the failure IS the passing evidence.
expect-runtime-fail: Message 'serial' not understood by receiver
*)
class SerialConfinedTest usingPlatform: platform = () (
  public main: platform2 args: args = (
    serial write: 'oops'.
    'SHOULD NOT REACH' println.
    ^ 0
  )
) : (
  public packageUsing: manifest = ( ^ self new )
)
